33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the bills change so much between summer and winter! And some rooms are way colder. We can't just split everything equally, right?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The fluctuations are significant. However, installing sub-meters would cost us over 170,000 yen total. That's a huge upfront cost for us to consider.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,I looked into the templates and other houses... and it sounds like a nightmare! It takes forever to do the math every single month!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's quite clear now. Some of us are indeed ""carrying"" others. One room is using four times the electricity of another. That's hardly a ""fair"" split.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The logs show we've had a lot of friction. We've been late with payments and arguing over small amounts for months. The tension is the real cost.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, if we just focus on the numbers, will we all end up freezing in our rooms because we're scared of the bill?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, that's why we need a balanced approach. We can't afford the electrician, but we can't ignore the winter spikes either.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Misaki, if we keep arguing, it's because the person doing the math is tired! We need a way that doesn't take an hour of someone's night!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, rationality doesn't mean freezing. It means the person running a space heater 24/7 pays for that luxury, rather than the person who doesn't.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, the problem isn't the time spent on math. It's that the reminders are being taken as accusations. We're avoiding each other over money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I just don't want us to be afraid to turn on the heat! Let's make sure the rule is clear so nobody feels guilty for being cold.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We need a system that accounts for the seasonal spikes without requiring a massive investment in hardware. A fixed monthly average might work.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But who has to do the work? If we have a ""system,"" someone still has to be the ""money person."" I don't want that to be a chore!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,A fixed average is a lazy solution. It ignores the actual usage. We should use a base fee plus a usage-based adjustment for the heavy hitters.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we go with a complex usage-based system, we'll just spend more time arguing over the ""adjustments."" I'd prefer something simple and transparent.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,Let's just make sure we talk about it openly! I'm okay with a bit of math if it means we all feel comfortable in our rooms.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm cautious about any system that doesn't account for the winter peak. If we don't plan for February, we'll be in trouble again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting for whatever is the fastest to finish! I want us to play games and hang out, not stare at spreadsheets!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll support any option that stops the ""carrying"" problem. It's an inefficient way to run a household and breeds resentment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I'll support the option that minimizes the need for ""reminders"" and ""queries."" Let's stop the cycle of accusation and avoidance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
