60,3,1,talk,Mio,,I like Option A! It means we know what to expect and we can just be cozy without worrying every single day!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is too expensive upfront. Option C is what we've been doing, and it's clearly not working for the budget. I prefer Option A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A sounds like the least amount of work! We only have to do the big math once a year instead of every single month!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the only truly fair one, but the cost is prohibitive. Option A is a compromise, provided the ""settlement"" at the end is strictly enforced.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A removes the monthly friction. No more monthly reminders that feel like attacks. We deal with the discrepancy once, and we're done.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, as long as we all agree on the ""settlement"" part, it'll be great! We can even have a party when we settle up!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, let's keep the party separate from the finances. I just want to ensure we set aside enough each month so the year-end isn't a shock.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that's a great idea! If we save a little extra, the ""big math"" day won't be scary!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, exactly. A calculated average based on the last twelve statements would make the year-end adjustment minimal. It's the most logical path.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. It shifts the focus from ""who spent what this month"" to ""how do we manage our shared budget."" It's much healthier for the house.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we're all agreeing! I can finally stop wearing my coat in the living room!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It's a reasonable compromise. It avoids the high cost of meters while providing more stability than a flat monthly split.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"Yay! Less math, more fun! I'm definitely voting for the one that lets us stop talking about bills!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"While it doesn't perfectly solve the usage disparity, it's the only viable option that doesn't bankrupt us or keep us in a state of constant conflict.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It's the best way to stop the money from souring our relationships. Let's move forward with this.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
